WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.235
- Hello everyone.

00:00:01.235 --> 00:00:04.138
Welcome to another
episode of Unlocking Lily.

00:00:04.138 --> 00:00:06.574
It's always been my dream to be a speaker,

00:00:06.574 --> 00:00:09.152
which led me to quit my day job to work

00:00:09.152 --> 00:00:11.470
and mentor under Evan full time

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.637
and all of you are coming
along for the ride with me.

00:00:17.558 --> 00:00:20.083
In every episode I take
on a different challenge

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:23.036
to really help me grow as a speaker.

00:00:23.036 --> 00:00:25.512
In this video I'm gunna be taking on

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.890
the biggest challenge yet.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.690
I'm gunna be doing my first TEDx Talk

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.664
and all of you are coming
on the road trip with me.

00:00:33.664 --> 00:00:35.622
Matter of fact, I'm leaving right now

00:00:35.622 --> 00:00:38.887
so I'm gunna see you guys
on the road very, very soon.

00:00:38.887 --> 00:00:41.470
(upbeat music)

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.374
We just arrived in Michigan.

00:00:47.374 --> 00:00:50.110
It's about 11:30 at night.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.829
We're gunna go check into the hotel.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:56.136
The lovely people at TEDx actually offered

00:00:56.136 --> 00:00:59.656
to pay for our hotel stay
which was really nice of them

00:00:59.656 --> 00:01:02.297
and surprising since it's
a non profit organization,

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:05.443
so super nice coming out of their pockets.

00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:10.214
We'll go check out this
hotel and catch you soon.

00:01:10.214 --> 00:01:11.885
(upbeat music)

00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:13.813
I've checked in, this is our room.

00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:15.741
It's quite nice and comfy.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:16.852
Tomorrow's a big day.

00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:19.762
We're gunna have a dress rehearsal.

00:01:19.762 --> 00:01:23.306
It's getting kind of late
so we're gunna change

00:01:23.306 --> 00:01:24.802
and go to sleep.

00:01:24.802 --> 00:01:28.566
(light piano music)

00:01:28.566 --> 00:01:29.399
- We're just getting, honestly,

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:31.541
I'm gunna find this
place by using the sun.

00:01:31.541 --> 00:01:35.482
- We're trying to figure out
how to get to the TEDx place

00:01:35.482 --> 00:01:37.331
because we have no GPS, and...

00:01:37.331 --> 00:01:38.359
- We have no GPS

00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:40.543
- None of our internet
connection is working

00:01:40.543 --> 00:01:44.440
so we're going to try to get
there by following the sun.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.273
- By following the sun.

00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:46.604
- Yes, yes.

00:01:46.604 --> 00:01:47.437
- Sun dial.

00:01:47.437 --> 00:01:48.990
- Yes.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.333
Hopefully we get there soon,

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.592
before my dress rehearsal starts

00:01:51.592 --> 00:01:53.278
but it's gunna be interesting.

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:54.422
- We have no idea what road we're on.

00:01:54.422 --> 00:01:55.934
- We'll see.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.543
We'll see.

00:01:57.543 --> 00:01:58.626
Ah, TEDx.

00:01:58.626 --> 00:01:59.820
Here we go.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.403
(upbeat music)

00:02:07.209 --> 00:02:10.853
So we finally made it to the
Livonia Civic Center Library

00:02:10.853 --> 00:02:13.774
where the TEDx event is
gunna be taking place.

00:02:13.774 --> 00:02:14.809
I'm feeling good.

00:02:14.809 --> 00:02:17.454
I'm not feeling nervous quite yet.

00:02:17.454 --> 00:02:19.520
Maybe cause it feels...

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.547
Surreal.

00:02:20.547 --> 00:02:22.801
It doesn't feel like it's real.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:25.433
So we're gunna go in and
maybe the nerves will kick in

00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:28.157
or maybe I might not get nervous at all.

00:02:28.157 --> 00:02:30.740
(upbeat music)

00:02:41.357 --> 00:02:44.573
Hey everyone, I just
finished my dress rehearsal.

00:02:44.573 --> 00:02:46.589
I was so nervous.

00:02:46.589 --> 00:02:48.150
Oh my God.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.303
I was speaking really fast
and I couldn't figure out

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:55.450
the clicker thing, oh my
goodness, and I'm so glad

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.727
that I had this rehearsal
cause I feel like I got

00:02:57.727 --> 00:03:00.083
all my nerves out of
the way and now I know

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:02.263
how I'm gunna do things differently.

00:03:02.263 --> 00:03:04.137
Yeah, I just didn't expect it.

00:03:04.137 --> 00:03:05.589
I was just kind of sitting
back there thinking

00:03:05.589 --> 00:03:08.579
that I got this, I practiced
it about two hundred times

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:11.642
and it's so different
when you're up there.

00:03:11.642 --> 00:03:12.791
Gosh.

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:14.925
I think it's gunna be a
lot better tomorrow tho.

00:03:14.925 --> 00:03:17.730
I think so but people
are super supportive.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.021
They were so nice and
they did the exercises

00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:21.452
I asked them to do.

00:03:21.452 --> 00:03:22.285
It was all good,

00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:26.188
but tomorrow's gunna be
a lot better than today.

00:03:26.188 --> 00:03:29.439
(uplifting piano music)

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:31.316
So today is the day.

00:03:31.316 --> 00:03:33.524
I'm just getting ready to leave.

00:03:33.524 --> 00:03:35.077
I'm really excited.

00:03:35.077 --> 00:03:36.077
I'm really, really excited.

00:03:36.077 --> 00:03:37.393
I'm not nervous.

00:03:37.393 --> 00:03:40.475
I am excited and this
morning I was just listening

00:03:40.475 --> 00:03:43.608
to some music that made
me feel in a pumped

00:03:43.608 --> 00:03:46.741
and a ready to go and
feeling extraordinary

00:03:46.741 --> 00:03:49.664
and I'm just thinking about
when I'm gunna be on stage

00:03:49.664 --> 00:03:50.621
and how it's gunna be

00:03:50.621 --> 00:03:54.606
and I really don't want it to end at all.

00:03:54.606 --> 00:03:56.854
I feel like they have
to pry me off the stage

00:03:56.854 --> 00:03:57.812
at the 18 minute mark.

00:03:57.812 --> 00:03:59.045
We'll see, we'll see.

00:03:59.045 --> 00:04:01.192
I'll try to linger as long as possible.

00:04:01.192 --> 00:04:02.980
It's, you know, it's something
that I've been working on

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.839
for such a long time
and it's finally here.

00:04:05.839 --> 00:04:08.282
I don't want it to be over so quickly.

00:04:08.282 --> 00:04:11.727
Well, I'll catch you guys
soon when I do my speech.

00:04:11.727 --> 00:04:14.560
(uplifting music)

00:04:25.966 --> 00:04:28.299
So it's nine minutes before showtime.

00:04:28.299 --> 00:04:30.858
I'm gunna be taking on
the stage very, very soon.

00:04:30.858 --> 00:04:32.619
I have to be quiet
because it's quiet here.

00:04:32.619 --> 00:04:35.452
(uplifting music)

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.456
Hello, everyone, so it's about 8 o'clock.

00:04:55.456 --> 00:04:57.485
We're wrapped up TEDx Talk.

00:04:57.485 --> 00:05:01.648
The first TEDx Talk ever that
I have done which was amazing.

00:05:01.648 --> 00:05:03.610
It went really well.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.982
It went better that I thought
which was quite amazing

00:05:06.982 --> 00:05:09.587
cause I thought I would be pretty awesome

00:05:09.587 --> 00:05:12.815
and it actually went
better than I thought.

00:05:12.815 --> 00:05:16.254
I'm gunna try to digest everything
that has happened today.

00:05:16.254 --> 00:05:17.935
I'm gunna think about it tonight,

00:05:17.935 --> 00:05:20.867
think about it tomorrow
morning on our way home

00:05:20.867 --> 00:05:24.521
and we're gunna go back to
the hotel, catch some snooze

00:05:24.521 --> 00:05:28.747
and we're gunna be heading
back to Toronto very soon.

00:05:28.747 --> 00:05:29.688
Oh, this is Evan.

00:05:29.688 --> 00:05:31.316
Believe.

00:05:31.316 --> 00:05:34.711
(upbeat music)

00:05:34.711 --> 00:05:36.863
So I am back from my TEDx Talk.

00:05:36.863 --> 00:05:39.974
I'm just thinking about
all the great things

00:05:39.974 --> 00:05:41.995
that happened during the conference.

00:05:41.995 --> 00:05:46.174
The organizers working so hard,
tirelessly around the clock

00:05:46.174 --> 00:05:48.111
to make sure everything ran smoothly.

00:05:48.111 --> 00:05:50.401
The speaker's were awesome.

00:05:50.401 --> 00:05:53.173
They had such great things to share

00:05:53.173 --> 00:05:55.404
and I feel like I learned a lot from them

00:05:55.404 --> 00:05:57.434
and we also made a
connection so we're gunna

00:05:57.434 --> 00:06:00.299
keep in contact with
each other for a while,

00:06:00.299 --> 00:06:01.132
and the audience.

00:06:01.132 --> 00:06:05.513
The audience, they were so
supportive and they came up to me

00:06:05.513 --> 00:06:07.730
after my talk and we had conversations

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.812
and I made some connections there as well

00:06:09.812 --> 00:06:12.369
so I'm super grateful in all the things

00:06:12.369 --> 00:06:14.952
that happened during the talk

00:06:14.952 --> 00:06:19.487
and now, thinking back to my
own talk, I thought I'd share

00:06:19.487 --> 00:06:22.512
three things that went really well for me

00:06:22.512 --> 00:06:25.724
and three things that I could improve on.

00:06:25.724 --> 00:06:27.736
So I'm gunna start off by
telling you three things

00:06:27.736 --> 00:06:29.370
that I did really well.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.710
Number one, is I maintained
within the time limit.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:36.682
As a speaker, you're always
gunna be given a certain amount

00:06:36.682 --> 00:06:39.035
of time that your speech
is supposed to be.

00:06:39.035 --> 00:06:42.037
So in the TEDx world, your
speech cannot be longer

00:06:42.037 --> 00:06:43.370
than 18 minutes.

00:06:44.332 --> 00:06:47.070
So for me, I was particularly nervous

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:49.849
because weeks leading up to my talk,

00:06:49.849 --> 00:06:53.056
my speech was still about
20 minutes long or so,

00:06:53.056 --> 00:06:56.131
so it took me a lot of
practice and editing it down

00:06:56.131 --> 00:06:58.158
and cutting it back and back and back

00:06:58.158 --> 00:07:00.003
and practice, practice, practice

00:07:00.003 --> 00:07:03.045
to finally get it down to 18 minutes.

00:07:03.045 --> 00:07:06.096
Number two, is engaging the audience.

00:07:06.096 --> 00:07:09.216
I wanted to create a talk
that was more conversational

00:07:09.216 --> 00:07:11.833
and more interactive so
I got them to do stuff

00:07:11.833 --> 00:07:13.180
like hugging each other.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:16.117
I got them to raise their
hands when I asked a question.

00:07:16.117 --> 00:07:20.190
I even got them to answer
one question for me.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.332
It was really high risk
because the potential

00:07:23.332 --> 00:07:26.265
of it going wrong was highly likely.

00:07:26.265 --> 00:07:28.547
There could have been
a complete dead silence

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:30.731
and nobody answering my
questions or everyone reluctant

00:07:30.731 --> 00:07:33.960
to raise their hands but I
went in with so much conviction

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.381
because it's something
that I really wanted to do

00:07:36.381 --> 00:07:38.992
to kind of draw the audience in to kind of

00:07:38.992 --> 00:07:41.161
be part of my talk rather
than just observing

00:07:41.161 --> 00:07:44.028
that it ended up working
out really well for me.

00:07:44.028 --> 00:07:47.518
Number three is my emotional commitment.

00:07:47.518 --> 00:07:51.693
Whether it was sadness,
frustration, happiness, all of that,

00:07:51.693 --> 00:07:54.501
I committed myself fully into it.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:57.020
This is the part I struggle with the most

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.328
when I was going through
the practice sessions.

00:07:59.328 --> 00:08:03.073
I was telling the stories,
I wasn't feeling it

00:08:03.073 --> 00:08:06.377
and I'm so glad I put in the
extra time to really practice

00:08:06.377 --> 00:08:08.089
over and over again that I was really able

00:08:08.089 --> 00:08:11.177
to get the emotions out as well.

00:08:11.177 --> 00:08:13.192
Now the three areas of improvement.

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.439
Number one, PowerPoint.

00:08:15.439 --> 00:08:19.025
Oh my goodness, I totally
underestimated the power

00:08:19.025 --> 00:08:20.396
of PowerPoints.

00:08:20.396 --> 00:08:23.217
It really captivates
the audience if you have

00:08:23.217 --> 00:08:24.588
a nice visual presentation

00:08:24.588 --> 00:08:26.676
to go along with your voice as well.

00:08:26.676 --> 00:08:30.513
I didn't spend nearly
enough time as I should have

00:08:30.513 --> 00:08:32.549
practicing with a PowerPoint as well as

00:08:32.549 --> 00:08:36.211
investing into making the
PowerPoints visually stunning.

00:08:36.211 --> 00:08:39.502
So definitely next time around,
practice, practice, practice

00:08:39.502 --> 00:08:41.841
with a PowerPoint, for
sure, for sure, for sure.

00:08:41.841 --> 00:08:43.758
Number two is my voice.

00:08:44.622 --> 00:08:48.622
I didn't realize how quiet I
was being on stage until I saw

00:08:48.622 --> 00:08:50.275
the video of myself speaking.

00:08:50.275 --> 00:08:53.382
I could have definitely
projected my voice a lot further

00:08:53.382 --> 00:08:56.374
than I did and also the
variation of my voice,

00:08:56.374 --> 00:08:57.575
I could have played around with the speed

00:08:57.575 --> 00:08:59.808
and the tempo of it,
which could have made it

00:08:59.808 --> 00:09:01.949
more interesting for people to hear

00:09:01.949 --> 00:09:04.591
so lots and lots of vocal lessons for me

00:09:04.591 --> 00:09:07.787
to get my voice up there for my next talk.

00:09:07.787 --> 00:09:10.964
Number three is a stronger ending.

00:09:10.964 --> 00:09:13.187
There wasn't anything wrong
with the words that I used,

00:09:13.187 --> 00:09:17.004
but I could have brought way
more conviction that I did

00:09:17.004 --> 00:09:19.340
for the call to action in the end.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.459
The whole reason why
I want to be a speaker

00:09:21.459 --> 00:09:25.535
is to spark a change in people
and for people to take action

00:09:25.535 --> 00:09:29.997
after hearing my talk so if
I brought way more confidence

00:09:29.997 --> 00:09:32.464
and way more conviction
in the end I feel like

00:09:32.464 --> 00:09:35.735
more people will be willing to
go out there and take action.

00:09:35.735 --> 00:09:39.519
So I had quite a few people
ask me how I got my TEDx Talk.

00:09:39.519 --> 00:09:42.925
So for my next challenge, I'm
going to share with all of you

00:09:42.925 --> 00:09:45.627
how I landed my first TEDx talk.

00:09:45.627 --> 00:09:46.958
So the question of the day is:

00:09:46.958 --> 00:09:50.990
what is your one big goal that
you're working on right now?

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.613
Write in the comments below

00:09:52.613 --> 00:09:54.616
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:09:54.616 --> 00:09:56.897
I have a special shout
out for Donna Osborn.

00:09:56.897 --> 00:10:00.834
Donna Osborn wrote "you're
Amazing, Lily! You inspire me

00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:03.524
to work on making my own Magic happen

00:10:03.524 --> 00:10:05.796
and move away from playing it safe."

00:10:05.796 --> 00:10:07.873
Yes, Donna, thank you so much for writing

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:10.601
that beautiful comment
and that's what we want.

00:10:10.601 --> 00:10:13.537
We want you to make more magic happen.

00:10:13.537 --> 00:10:14.405
Thanks again, Donna.

00:10:14.405 --> 00:10:16.804
So thank you so much for
watching, and more importantly

00:10:16.804 --> 00:10:18.429
being on this journey with me.

00:10:18.429 --> 00:10:21.181
Some of you have been
with me since day one.

00:10:21.181 --> 00:10:25.804
It's crazy and I really
hope that I get to meet you

00:10:25.804 --> 00:10:29.433
in person one day so I get
to give you a big giant hug

00:10:29.433 --> 00:10:32.092
to thank you for all the
love and support you've been

00:10:32.092 --> 00:10:36.259
giving me so far and I will
see you very, very soon.

